{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnU5EnWCEN2G9igd1kP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a Vitest 5 breaking change. Browser mode now turns on `locators.exact` by default, so `getByText('Save')` only matches an element whose text is exactly \"Save\". It no longer finds \"Save changes\" through a partial match. The v5.0.0 release notes list this under browser breaking changes as \"Enable `locators.exact` by default\". They don't explain the option any further, so the exact-match behavior is what the option name and the old Testing Library semantics suggest.\n\nTo fix it, you can do any of these:\n- Use the full text: `getByText('Save changes')`.\n- Opt out for one call: `getByText('Save', { exact: false })`.\n- Use a regex: `getByText(/Save/)`.\n- Restore the old default for the whole project: set `test.browser.locators.exact: false` in your config.\n\nSource: [Vitest v5.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":5402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"055a1eb5-8557-40f1-8438-b8ed95e13081","uuid":"dd92082f-ea7e-41eb-8dca-7310e1f20ef8","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:40.718Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnU4xfUdabuiiNX3aTh"}
